timeline.body:
How about:
```
boolean nativeToolchainNeed = !ImageSingletons.contains(LLVMFeature.class)
if (nativeToolchainNeed) {
    CCompilerInvoker compilerInvoker = CCompilerInvoker.create(tempDirectory());
    compilerInvoker.verifyCompiler();
    ImageSingletons.add(CCompilerInvoker.class, compilerInvoker);
}
```
Not sure it makes sense to bring `ExitAfterRelocatableImageWrite` in. Even with ExitAfterRelocatableImageWrite you still need a native toolchain for query code compilation, or am I missing something?

Instead of `"llvm".equals(SubstrateOptions.CompilerBackend.getValue())` I'd use `ImageSingletons.contains(LLVMFeature.class)` wherever possible.

